<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Benjamín Zeledón</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1879–1912</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Benjamín Zeledón was a Nicaraguan lawyer, politician and general who led a Liberal rising in 1912 against the Conservative government of Adolfo Díaz. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Marines landed to support the government, and Zeledón was killed in October 1912 after the fall of his positions near Masaya. He is remembered as a national hero of resistance to American intervention and an inspiration to the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augusto-cesar-sandino">Augusto César Sandino</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/benjamin-zeledon.jpg" alt="Benjamín Zeledón" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Kazama182~commonswiki assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_benjamin_zeledon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
